  VERDICT FOR THE PAIR: THE AAP'S ANCHORED EXPECTATION IS UNMET - THIS PAIR IS
  NON-DISCRIMINATING ON THE MANDATED SUBJECT. AAP 0.5.1 and 0.9.1 expect one
  traced finding at line 72 with taint on and ZERO with it off. Observed by
  this run at the pinned root, one rule, one file: 1 finding(s) at line(s) 72
  with the flag and 1 at line(s) 72 without it, and the two arms' SARIF
  outputs are BYTE-IDENTICAL - 4753 bytes each, sha256
  7949617b3c88edba9faec24b79c7256667c59cf00885aadb8bd12da099845778. A contrast
  of zero is not a contrast, so the anchor is NOT met and nothing in this file
  claims that it was.

  WHY, established from the engine's own option list and this run's own trace
  rather than from speculation. Of the 110 long options Opengrep 1.27.1
  exposes, exactly TWO have a name that mentions taint and NEITHER of them
  disables taint analysis - APPENDIX C carries the list and the measurement
  verbatim. --taint-intrafile only ADDS intra-file inter-procedural taint, and
  its own help text says the fallback is 'intraprocedural analysis only'. On
  this subject the rule's source and its sink sit inside ONE method - the
  parameter is declared at line 64 (def put(blockId: BlockId)) and the sink is
  the interpolated string at line 72 - so the flow never crosses a method
  boundary, the default intraprocedural taint analysis already reaches it, and
  the flag has nothing left to contribute. 'Taint off' therefore means
  'intraprocedural taint' rather than 'no taint', and a truly taint-free arm
  is NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE with this engine at this pin.

  SO THE UNMET ANCHOR IS AN AAP DIVERGENCE CAUSED BY THE ENGINE'S OPTION
  SURFACE, not a harness defect and not something a rewording repairs. AAP
  0.9.2 makes 'a failed taint A/B' a halt-class condition, so it is recorded
  here as one: reported and NOT repaired, and propagated into oss-scan-
  results/run-record.md, oss-scan-results/tool-status.md and oss-scan-
  results/build-record.md rather than being left in this file alone. What it
  is not is a defect engineering can close - the two arms already differ only
  in the taint setting, which is what the pass condition requires, and no
  runner, rule or ruleset may be edited (AAP 0.8.1). No rule, file, line or
  flag was changed to manufacture a contrast.

  WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, AS A FIRST-HAND MEASUREMENT OF THIS RUN: the HiveShim
  pair (harness/artifacts/logs/taint-ab-hiveshim-on.log and taint-ab-hiveshim-
  off.log), re-run by this run at this same pinned root with the same pinned
  rule, the same engine and --taint-intrafile as the only analysis difference,
  produced 2 traced finding(s) at lines 828, 834 with taint on and 0 with it
  off, each trace crossing method boundaries (source 'predicates' at line 351
  -> call 'convertFilters' at 351 -> propagator 'filters' at 645 -> propagator
  'flatMap' at 861 -> sink at 828 / 834). That is exactly the shape the AAP
